    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.55,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"polarity\",\n      \"components\": [\"D3\", \"T3\", \"R7\", \"T5\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"D3.1\", \"D3.2\", \"T3.1\", \"T3.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"/D_{ATO}\", \"GND\", \"/+24V_{F}\"],\n      \"observed\": \"D3 (12 V zener) has its cathode (pin 1, K) on the ATO gate node /D_{ATO} and its anode (pin 2, A) on GND. T3 is a P-channel MOSFET whose source (pin 2, S) is on /+24V_{F} and whose gate (pin 1, G) is on /D_{ATO}. R7 pulls the gate up to the source rail.\",\n      \"expected\": \"A gate-protection zener for a P-channel high-side switch should clamp the gate relative to its source (+24V_{F}), not to ground. With the cathode on the gate and the anode on GND, the zener clamps the gate to about 12 V whenever T5 is off, giving Vgs of about -12 V and keeping T3 on, so the ATO valve would stay energised. When T5 is on, the gate sits near 0 V, giving Vgs of about -24 V, which exceeds a typical \u00b120 V gate rating.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"39\\\") (name \\\"/D_{ATO}\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"D3\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"K\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"T3\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"G\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"75\\\") (name \\\"GND\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"D3\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"6\\\") (name \\\"/+24V_{F}\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"T3\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"S\\\") (pintype \\\"power_in\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"T3 \u2014 AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The ATO solenoid valve may be held open continuously, or the T3 gate may be overstressed when the valve is commanded off or on. Either way, the top-off valve control does not behave as intended.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"U1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U1.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The TPS62933 enable pin (U1 pin 2, EN) is marked no-connect and is not tied to VIN, a divider or any logic net.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The TPS62933 EN pin should be tied to a defined level, for example VIN through a resistor divider, so the 24 V to 5 V buck is reliably enabled. A floating EN pin can leave the regulator disabled or make its start-up undefined.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"135\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"EN\\\") (pintype \\\"input+no_connect\\\")))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"U1 \u2014 TPS62933 (TI) | 24 V \u2192 5 V synchronous buck regulator, 3 A\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the part has no internal pull-up on EN, the 5 V rail and everything it powers (ESP32 5V0, the LDO and the 3.3 V rail) may never start. The spec does not document this as intentional.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The most likely anomaly is the gate-protection zener D3, whose anode is on GND rather than on the +24 V source, which would hold the P-channel ATO valve switch T3 on and overstress its gate. The floating TPS62933 EN pin is a weaker, lower-confidence concern.\"\n}",
